\f1\b0  Finding unlisted, high-quality small businesses with retiring founders is incredibly slow and manual.\
\ls2\ilvl1
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Industry Focus:
\f1\b0  IT Managed Service Providers (MSPs) in the US Midwest.\
\ls2\ilvl1
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Scoring Contract:
\f1\b0  Predicting a continuous investment-grade score from 
\f0\b 1.0 to 10.0
\f1\b0  (constrained to strict 0.5-point increments).\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Spoken Script (Simple & Direct):
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 "In a 'Search Fund,' an entrepreneur raises money to buy and run a single small business from a founder who wants to retire. Finding these hidden companies manually takes hundreds of hours of tedious digging. I focused my search on IT Managed Service Providers\'97or MSPs. I formalized this problem into a machine learning contract: our model must read a company's profile and predict an investment grade from 1 to 10 in strict 0.5 steps, perfectly mimicking a human investor's rubric."\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

