\f1\b0  Text features that tagged less than 16% of rows introduced extreme variance and noise.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Spoken Script (Simple & Direct):
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 "Over 22 automated runs, we organized our experiments into clear thematic paths. Early on, focusing on continuous numerical data gave us an incredible breakthrough, leading to our champion model, Experiment 009. After that, the agent tried to improve the model by scraping text from company websites\'97looking for things like whether a company was founder-led or already acquired. These text experiments consistently failed. We discovered a 'sparsity floor': when a text feature applies to less than 16% of our small dataset, it introduces massive mathematical variance, causing the model to overfit to single outlier companies."\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

