\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Spoken Script (Simple & Direct):
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 "Let\'92s look at what actually worked versus what failed. Two structural features drove our success. First, the 'Stagnation Premium': our model proved that 
\f2\i lower
\f1\i0  revenue-per-employee actually predicts a higher-quality target, because it mathematically captures operational slack that a new CEO can easily optimize. Second, the 'Succession Bell Curve': company age is non-linear, and target quality peaks right at the 20-year mark when a founder is hitting retirement age.\uc0\u8232 What failed completely was hunting for website keywords. In Experiment 016, the agent found a massive apparent 'win' by tracking the word 'compliance.' But a human audit revealed this was a fake statistical trap. The model wasn't finding better companies; it was just separating a small minority of companies that left generic marketing text off their website from the majority that included it. We caught this and discarded it to protect our model's real-world credibility."\
